## Recommendations

- Use one standard unit, such as kilograms, for bag weight.
- Use a consistent date format for harvest-year values.
- Maintain standardized region and processing-method names.
- Improve data collection for altitude, variety, and processing method.
- Add sensory quality variables such as aroma, flavor, acidity, defects, and total cup points for future coffee-quality analysis.

## Limitation

This dataset supports analysis of coffee certification, origin, altitude, processing methods, bag quantities, and certification patterns.

It does not include sensory-quality variables such as aroma, flavor, acidity, defects, or total cup points. Therefore, this project does not rank coffee quality.

## Conclusion

This project demonstrates an end-to-end EDA workflow using Arabica coffee certification data. It shows how raw records can be cleaned, explored, and transformed into useful insights about coffee origin, altitude, processing practices, and certification trends.
